verses.text:
Kings of the earth line up for battle.
Rulers meet together in secret
against Yahweh and the king he chose.{b}

Let me announce what Yahweh decided.
He told me, “You are my son.
Today is the day I became your father.{d}

Many say about me,
“God will not come to save him.”
Selah{b}

Answer me when I call, my God who does right!
You gave me room when I was in a tight spot.{b}
Have pity on me and listen as I pray.

Yahweh, our Lord,{b}
how glorious your name is over all the earth!
Your splendor is set high above the sky.{c}

From the mouths of children and babies
you have built a stronghold against your enemies,
to stop the foe who wants revenge.{d}

so I can tell of all your praises
and celebrate your rescue
at the gates of the daughter of Zion.{c}

I have made Yahweh my safe place.
So why do you say to me,
“Fly off to the hills like a bird!”{b}

The promises of Yahweh are clean and pure,
like silver melted in a clay oven{b}
and cleaned seven times over.

Every one has turned away. Together they have gone bad.
Nobody does good.
Not even one.{c}

He lends money without charging interest.{a}
He cannot be paid to hurt an innocent person.
Whoever lives this way will never be shaken.

Yahweh thundered in the sky.
The Most High let his voice be heard,
with hail and fiery coals.{e}

When you appear, you will turn them into a blazing oven.{b}
Yahweh in his anger will gulp them down,
and flames will eat them up.

My God, my God, why did you leave me alone?{b}
Why are you so far away when I need help,
so far from my groans?{c}

They say, “He leaves his troubles with Yahweh.{d}
Let Yahweh save him!
Let him rescue the man he likes so much!”

Dogs are all around me.
A gang of evil men has closed me in.
They have stabbed through my hands and feet.{h}

All the wealthy people of the earth will feast and bow down.
All who are going down to the dust will kneel before him,
even those who cannot keep themselves alive.{n}

He restores my strength.
He guides me down the right roads,{b}
because that is who he is.

Even when I go through the darkest valley,{c}
I am not afraid of harm, since you are with me.
Your club and your walking stick calm my fears.

Such are the people who come looking for him,{b}
who seek your face, God of Jacob.{c}
Selah

Yahweh’s voice makes deer give birth{f}
and strips the forests bare.
In his temple everyone shouts, “Glory!”

Day and night your hand pressed down on me.
My strength dried up like a field in a summer drought.{c}
Selah

But when they were ill, I put on sackcloth.
I humbled myself by going without food.
My prayer came back to me unanswered.{c}

Sin whispers to the wicked person
deep in his heart.{a}
He has no fear of God in front of his eyes.{b}

But the wicked will die.
Yahweh’s enemies will vanish like flowers in a meadow.{d}
They will go up in smoke and be gone.

I stayed completely silent.
I said nothing, even though it did no good,{b}
and my pain only got worse.

Yahweh will guard him and preserve his life.
He will be called happy in the land,{a}
and you will not leave him to his enemies’ desires.

Even my close friend, the one I trusted,
who ate at my table,
has lifted his heel against me.{d}

Praise to Yahweh, Israel’s God,
from age to age!
Amen and Amen.{e}

Tears are my only food by day and by night,
while people keep asking me,
“Where is your God?”

My God, my soul is low inside me.
So I think of you from the land of the Jordan,
from the peaks of Hermon, from Mount Mizar.{c}

My enemies taunt me, and it feels like my bones are breaking.{d}
All day they ask me,
“Where is your God?”

In your majesty, ride out to victory
for the sake of truth, humility, and fairness.{c}
May your right hand do astonishing things.

Tell them: this is the God
who is ours for all time.
He will lead us even past death.{b}

“Look at the man who would not make God his fortress.
He trusted his great wealth
and grew strong by doing harm!”{c}

If only Israel’s rescue would come from Zion!
When God brings his people back from captivity,{c}
Jacob will celebrate and Israel will be glad.

Let death surprise them.
Let them go down alive into the grave.{b}
Evil lives in their homes, right in the middle of them.

He bought my life back and gave me peace
from the battle against me,
though so many are against me.

Wake up, my soul!{b}
Wake up, harp and lyre!
I will wake the dawn.

For the sin of their mouths and what their lips say,
let them be caught in their own pride,
and for the curses and lies they tell.

You gave a banner to those who fear you,
to wave because of the truth.{d}
Selah

God has spoken from his holy place:{f}
“I will celebrate. I will divide up Shechem
and measure out the Valley of Succoth.

Moab is my washbasin.
Over Edom I toss my sandal.{g}
Over Philistia I shout in triumph.”

They cheer each other on in their evil plan.
They talk about setting traps in secret.
They say, “Who will notice?”{a}

He changed the sea into dry land.
Our people walked through the river.{a}
We celebrated him there.

You let men ride over our heads.
We walked through flames and floods,
and then you brought us out into abundance.{c}

May God have pity on us and bless us,
and let his face shine on us.{a}
Selah

Sing to God. Make music for his name.
Build a road for the one who rides across the deserts.{b}
His name is Yah.{c} Celebrate in front of him.

the earth shook, and the sky poured rain
in front of God, the God of Sinai,{d}
in front of God, the God of Israel.

Even while you lie down among the sheep pens,{g}
a dove’s wings are covered with silver,
and her feathers shine with green-gold.

You climbed up high and led captives away.
You received gifts from people,
even from rebels, so that Yah God could live there.{k}

Rebuke the beast in the reeds,{o}
the herd of bulls and the calves of the nations.
They stomp on those who love silver.{p}
Scatter the peoples who enjoy war.

I have leaned on you since before I was born.
You are the one who took me from my mother’s body.{b}
I will always praise you.

May his glorious name be praised forever.
May his glory fill every corner of the earth.
Amen and amen.{f}

when God’s anger flared against them.
He killed the strongest of them
and struck down Israel’s young men.{g}

Do not charge us with the guilt of our ancestors.{a}
Let your tender love hurry to meet us,
because we have sunk so low.

Let the sighs of the prisoners reach you.
With your great strength,
keep alive those who are marked for death.{b}

He gave it as a law to Joseph
when he went out to fight{c} Egypt.
I heard a voice I had never heard:{d}

Assyria has also joined them.
They have become the strong arm{b} of the children of Lot.{c}
Selah

Passing through the Valley of Baca,{b}
they turn it into a spring-filled place.
The early rain wraps it in blessings.{c}

Protect my life, because I am loyal to you.{a}
You are my God. Save your servant,
who trusts in you.

Yahweh, God of Armies,
who is as strong as you, Yah?{c}
Your faithfulness surrounds you.

Who can live without ever seeing death?
Who can save his life from the grave’s power?{h}
Selah

A thousand years, to you,
are like yesterday when it is over,
like a few hours of the night.{d}

Shame on all who serve carved images,
who brag about worthless idols.
All you gods, bow down to him.{a}

Mighty is the King who loves what is fair.{b}
You made fairness firm.
You have done what is fair and right in Jacob.

Know that Yahweh is God.
It is he who made us, and we are his.{b}
We are his people, his own flock.

But Yahweh’s faithful love lasts from forever to forever
for those who fear him,
and his goodness reaches their grandchildren,

so that they would follow his rules
and obey his teachings.
Hallelujah!{g}

Hallelujah!{a}
Thank Yahweh, because he is good.
His faithful love lasts forever.

and brought together from many lands,
from east and west,
from north and south.{b}

God has spoken from his holy place:{c}
“I will celebrate! I will divide up Shechem
and measure out the Valley of Succoth.

Here is what Yahweh told my lord:{a}
“Take the seat of honor at my right,
until your enemies are a footstool under your feet.”

Yahweh has taken an oath and will not go back on it:
“You are a priest forever,
of the kind that Melchizedek was.”{c}

Hallelujah!{a}
I will thank Yahweh with all my heart,
among honest people when they meet together.

Respect for Yahweh is where wisdom starts.{b}
All who follow his orders gain good understanding.
His praise lasts forever.

Hallelujah!{a}
Happy is the person who respects Yahweh
and loves to follow his commands.

He gives freely to the poor.{b}
His goodness stands forever,
and his strength will be lifted up with honor.

Hallelujah!{a}
Praise him, servants of Yahweh.
Praise the name of Yahweh.

But as for us, we will bless Yah
now and always.
Hallelujah!{b}

To Jerusalem the tribes climb, the tribes of Yah,
as Israel was ordered to do,{a}
to thank Yahweh’s name.

My frame was never hidden from you
as I was shaped in secret,
put together deep in the earth.{d}

Let burning coals fall on them.{b}
Throw them into a fire,
into deep pits they cannot climb out of.

Reach down your hand from above.
Pull me out and save me from the deep water,
from the hands of foreigners,

May our cattle be heavy with young.{c}
May no wall be broken, no one taken as a prisoner,
and no cry of distress sound in our streets.

Hallelujah!
Praise God in his holy place.
Praise him in the sky that shows his power.{a}
